Fidesz would need to collapse to under 25% of seats, which given the winner's-bonus mixed system requires losing decisively even the popular vote by a wide margin AND losing most single-member districts. Even with TISZA competitive/leading in polls, Fidesz retaining >50 seats is near-certain since even a losing Fidesz would likely still win 60-90+ seats given district-level advantages. Market at 92% seems reasonable, perhaps slightly conservative.

92 out of 100 times, Fidesz–KDNP wins above 50 seats.

